  "hindi": "गायक दाहिनी ओर रहते हुए स्तुति करते हैं; पक्षी, छोटे पक्षी, ऋतु-ऋतु के अनुसार बोलते हैं। वह दोनों वाणियाँ बोलता है, साम गाने वाले के समान, और गायत्र तथा त्रैष्टुभ के अनुरूप शोभित होता है।",
  "english": "The singers praise, keeping to the right; the birds, the small birds, speak in due season. He speaks both voices like a Sāman-chanter, and shines in accord with both the gāyatra and the triṣṭubh.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Uncertain. pradakṣiṇit abhi gṛṇanti: pradakṣiṇit read as \"keeping to the right\" and abhi as adverbial. kāravaḥ may be the birds themselves or human singers; vayaḥ and śakuntayaḥ both mean birds. The IAST vācaṷ corresponds to Devanagari vācau (accent mark in the glyph). sāmagā iva is read sāmagāḥ iva (nominative singular, consistent with vadati). anu rājati (\"shines after / in accord with\") is uncertain. gāyatra and triṣṭubh are metre names, kept as Sanskrit.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
