  "hindi": "हे पक्षी, उद्गाता के समान तुम साम गाते हो; ब्रह्मा के पुत्र के समान यज्ञ के सवनों में शंसन करते हो। बलवान बैल की तरह, बच्चों वाली मादाओं के पास जाकर, सब ओर से हमारे लिए, हे पक्षी, कल्याणकारी बोलो। हर ओर से हमारे लिए, हे पक्षी, पुण्यकारी बोलो।",
  "english": "Like an Udgātṛ priest, O bird, you sing a sāman; like a son of a Brahman you recite at the pressings. Like a vigorous bull, having approached those with young, speak out what is good to us from all sides, O bird. From every side, O bird, speak out what is auspicious to us.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Uncertain in places. brahmaputra: brahman may mean the Brahman priest or a sacred utterance; \"son of a Brahman\" is the literal reading. vājī rendered \"vigorous\"; \"stallion/prize-winner\" are alternatives. śiśumatīr apītyā is unclear (apītyā may be a gerund of api-√i or an instrumental noun): the translation is tentative. The unit has three printed lines; the third is a separate pāda.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
